('<h3>How the copy is made</h3><p>Sign readings: Dietrich &amp; Loretz 1975, with the other editions in the side panel. Which signs fall on RS 15.30 + 15.49 and which on RS 17.387, and where each lyric line runs over the edge onto the reverse, follow Laroche 1955 and 1968. The text is written in a spiral: each lyric line crosses the obverse, turns over the right edge and finishes on the reverse, which is why the reverse shows the two pieces the other way round. For l. 3 the turn is placed approximately. RUM and KIB have no Unicode glyph in the font used here and are drawn as □.</p>',
 '<h3>摹本是怎么做的</h3><p>符号释读依 Dietrich &amp; Loretz 1975，其他版本见弹出的说明框。哪些符号在 RS 15.30 + 15.49 上、哪些在 RS 17.387 上，以及每行歌词在哪里越过边缘转到背面，都依 Laroche 1955 和 1968。文本呈螺旋状书写：每行歌词横穿正面，绕过右边缘，在背面写完，所以背面上两块残片的左右位置是反过来的。第 3 行转到背面的位置是估计的。RUM 和 KIB 在所用字体里没有 Unicode 字形，画作 □。</p>'),
# appendix B
('<span class="kicker">Appendix B</span>', '<span class="kicker">附录 B</span>'),
('<h2>The other Hurrian pieces</h2>', '<h2>其他胡里语残片</h2>'),
('<p>h.6 is the only tablet complete enough to perform, but some thirty other pieces from the same find carry the same notation. Here they are in Laroche’s editions (PRU III, 1955, for h.2–h.5; Ugaritica V, 1968, for h.7–h.30) or in Dumbrill’s 2005 transliteration, which restores more, each run through a scholar’s h.6 rules so that the fragments can be heard on the same terms. Restorations are kept in brackets and played as written; in Laroche’s text a broken term is named only where the surviving signs allow a single reading.</p>',
 '<p>h.6 是唯一完整到可以演奏的泥板，但同一批出土物中还有三十来块残片用的是同样的记谱。这里可以选用 Laroche 的版本（h.2–h.5 见 PRU III，1955；h.7–h.30 见 Ugaritica V，1968），也可以选用补出更多的 Dumbrill 2005 转写，并用某位学者在 h.6 上的规则逐一演绎，让这些残片能在同样的条件下被听到。补出的部分保留方括号，照写出的样子演奏；在 Laroche 的文本里，残缺的术语只有在残存符号只容一种读法时才认定。</p>'),
